[84.488441, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe restart of the \u001b[1;36;40mpayments-api\u001b[0m deployment did not resolve the issue. The pods are still failing    \r\r\nwith the same error:                                                                                \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mCurrent State\u001b[0m                                                                                       \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mPods \u001b[1;36;40mpayments-api-56f659864c-28s2w\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40mpayments-api-56f659864c-dt6c9\u001b[0m are in the \u001b[1;36;40mError\u001b[0m state.     \r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe logs and events indicate the same root cause: the \u001b[1;36;40mDATABASE_URL\u001b[0m environment variable is not   \r\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mset, causing the container to exit with code \u001b[1;36;40m1\u001b[0m.                                                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mNext Steps\u001b[0m                                                                                          \r\r\n\r\r\nThe deployment spec must be updated to ensure the \u001b[1;36;40mDATABASE_URL\u001b[0m environment variable is correctly    \r\r\nset. This value is expected to come from the \u001b[1;36;40mpayments-db\u001b[0m Secret.                                    \r\r\n\r\r\nWould you like me to verify the \u001b[1;36;40mpayments-db\u001b[0m Secret or proceed with patching the deployment?         \r\r\n\u001b[?25h"]
